<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-L95) maps Laws 1-5 to equations, source figures and the Lean theorem loci; every Pass 3 function docstring states its PDE, boundary conditions and closed forms and names what it is NOT (3D FEM); the math-KG spec registers equations 4-5 with Lean code and code loci. Deductions: the WT generator constants (0.62, 1.25, 3.0, f_band = 0.95 - 0.85 m + 0.50 m^2) are tuned to the vendored benchmark series and cited to no source (L355-L370) (-5); T0 = PH/2 and the 0.97 tolerance in the inscribed-disk check are uncited heuristics (L753, L836) (-3); Panel D's empirical bars are hard-coded literals rather than read from the reference JSON (L1394, L1400) (-2); the v2 wording 'spring-remodeling' survives in the `generate_puzzle_cell_polygon` docstring (L275) although the WT branch no longer remodels springs (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py L1394–L1400: ref_L / ref_S literals duplicated from the JSON <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L1394-L1400>",
        "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py L355–L370: Fitted generator constants with no literature citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L355-L370>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: exact EDT R_LEC (L215-L265) and the Sapala Laplace proxy, a coupled ROP2-ROP6 RD system (L533-L662), and the new reduced periclinal membrane solver (L723-L838) whose discretisation is verified against the closed-form disk (z_max 0.9 %, mean strain 0.3 %, L900-L906) and whose inscribed-disk bound holds on all 18 footprints (L836), plus the depth strip with FD-vs-modal agreement (L1009-L1158). Deductions: the 'shell' is a uniform-tension Foppl membrane with an analytic edge boundary layer, not a bending-coupled 3D FEM shell, and T0 = PH/2 (L753), E = 300 MPa, nu = 0.3 and H = 15 um are assumptions (-5); the reduced mechanics contradicts the Laplace proxy the script headlines (ratio 1.73 vs 3.32, exponent 0.51 vs 1; L888-L889, L1677-L1683) and the discrepancy is reported but not resolved (-4); the WT footprint is a tuned band-plus-capsule construction (L349-L407) rather than Sapala's emergent spring-remodelling, and the RD wall displacement never feeds the polygon (-4); the v2 ribbon construction (aspect 18.7) shows the LEC pinning mechanism was previously achieved by elongation, so v2's 94 was over-credited (-2 carried as a correction)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py L329–L338: Comment documenting that the v2 WT construction was a 417 x 22 um ribbon (aspect 18.7) and the Pass 3 replacement; the LEC pinning is still geometric, not emergent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L329-L338>",
