<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1641-L1799) now reports 17 reference-anchored measurements: the 9 v2 metrics (WT R_LEC 11.39 vs 11.4 um, r = 0.986, RMSE 0.26 um; Laplace ratio 3.32; RD r = -0.99 / 0.9998; lambda 24.5 um; mature S 0.655 vs 0.68; ktn1 L 1.111 vs 1.11; specimen S 0.72) plus 8 Pass 3 metrics, of which the shell ratio (1.73 vs 3.32), the sigma-R_LEC exponent (0.51 vs 1) and r (0.98) are genuine tests against the paper's proxy. Deductions: five of the eight new measurements use analytic or model-internal references (disk closed form, inscribed-disk bound, FD-vs-modal error, analytic inner-face gain, junction-forcing control) — solver verification, not biological validation (-8); the depth attenuation has no empirical reference at all (-4); the mature WT lobeyness 1.734 is 0.11 above the 1.62 reference and the lobe count (12) is outside 7.8 +/- 1.6 but neither is reported as a measurement (-3); the specimen lobeyness differs from the v2 record (1.316 vs 1.506) with unchanged code, undermining it as a reference (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
