<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Judged on the regenerated PNG and GIF: the mature WT footprint (Panel B/G) is now a compact puzzle-like cell with alternating bulbous lobes and a LEC-setting neck band, visibly distinct from the isotropic disk, the ktn1 near-polygon and the monocot file cell, and the specimen panel (F) overlays 10 segmented cells with inscribed LEC circles. Deductions: the WT shape is schematic — a straight symmetric band with evenly pitched comb-like lobes and 12 lobes at maturity vs the reference 7.8 +/- 1.6 (L376, L355) (-6); the two youngest stages are a near-circle and a single-bump capsule (L = 1.004 and 1.075 vs 1.08 and 1.21) so early lobe initiation is under-rendered (-4); there is no side-by-side overlay of a model cell on a segmented specimen cell, and the specimen mean S = 0.72 vs model 0.655 is not discussed (-4); the depth field (Panel I) and the bulge field (Panel G) have no specimen or paper-figure counterpart to compare against (-4); the v2 ribbon (hidden by the +/-68 um clip of Panel B) means v2's 91 was over-credited (-2 carried)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
